1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,369
In eighteen seventy two, a ship crossed hundreds of miles of the Atlantic with nobody on board.

2
00:00:07,769 --> 00:00:13,465
The Mary Celeste's last log entry was written near the Azores, on November twenty fifth.

3
00:00:13,965 --> 00:00:18,406
Nine days later, she was found about four hundred nautical miles away.

4
00:00:18,626 --> 00:00:19,537
Still sailing.

5
00:00:19,757 --> 00:00:20,935
Completely empty.

6
00:00:21,435 --> 00:00:22,796
The lifeboat was gone.

7
00:00:23,016 --> 00:00:27,067
The food, the water, and the family's belongings were all still there.

8
00:00:28,468 --> 00:00:32,549
So the crew left in a hurry, and the ship just kept going without them.

9
00:00:33,249 --> 00:00:34,007
Honestly?

10
00:00:34,227 --> 00:00:36,358
Better navigation than me with a phone.

11
00:00:36,858 --> 00:00:39,841
Follow for more true stories history never finished.
